Subject: winemac.drv: deliver every mouse move (no AppKit coalescing)
Date: 2026-11-02
Applies to: CrossOver 26.3.0 Wine sources, after 0021
Files changed: dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m

AppKit coalesces mouse-moved events by default: the moves a mouse reports
between two display refreshes reach the program as one event, so a program
never gets more mouse events per second than the display refreshes. Games
read those moves as relative motion every frame; with a 500-1000 Hz mouse,
4-8 reports are merged per refresh and arrive in uneven batches against the
game's frames (also on CrossOver). The Mac driver now turns coalescing off
when it makes the process a foreground app, so every report arrives.
WINE_MOUSE_COALESCING=1 keeps AppKit's default.

Measured with a raw-input test program (cursor clipped and hidden, as the
games do) on a 120 Hz display with a 125 Hz mouse: 119-120 events/s with
coalescing (the refresh rate), 125/s without (every report), in each of four
runs. With a 125 Hz mouse that is a small gain; it grows with the mouse's
report rate. No extra cost was seen.

---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -336,6 +336,17 @@
                                                                 reason:@"Running Windows program"] retain]; // intentional leak
             }
 
+            /* AppKit coalesces mouse moves to at most one event per display
+             * refresh. Games read every move as relative motion, and a
+             * 500-1000 Hz mouse then arrives in uneven batches against the
+             * game's frames. Deliver every report unless
+             * WINE_MOUSE_COALESCING=1. */
+            {
+                const char *coalescing = getenv("WINE_MOUSE_COALESCING");
+                if (!coalescing || strcmp(coalescing, "1"))
+                    [NSEvent setMouseCoalescingEnabled:NO];
+            }
+
             mainMenu = [[[NSMenu alloc] init] autorelease];
 
             // Application menu
